I discarded the hypothesis that conditions alpha-up on alpha being high, because its condition is the edited field's own current value. None of the remaining conditions simply switch off the edited component.

I treated a field pair as unordered, so alpha/batch_size and batch_size/alpha count as the same pair. The remaining hypotheses cover only nine such pairs, so the list repeats one: batch_size with learning_rate_init. The two entries for that pair differ in which field is edited and in mechanism: one is about stability at high learning rates, the other about undertraining with large batches. For each other pair I kept the single hypothesis that seemed most open to a bet in either direction.

