"direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper ReLU stacks have sharper loss curvature and reach the edge of stability at smaller learning rates."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "width", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "Narrow nets are already capacity-bound, so additional shrinkage pushes them into underfitting faster than redundant wide nets."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "depth", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Shrinkage applied to every layer compounds multiplicatively through a three-layer stack, collapsing the signal more than in a single-layer net."}]}
